(a) The data dimensions and groups are ordered by importance independently. An iteration of the Monte Carlo tree search consists of four stages, including (b) selection, (c) expansion, (d) simulation, and (e) backpropagation. The shapes with a yellow frame represent the operation of this stage. Inside the nodes are element thumbnails (
    \$e_{i}\$
  ) or axes (
    \$\alpha_{i}\$
