A chart pair demonstrating constraint weight trade-offs. Despite higher weights for a linear x scale (weight = 0.469) and ordinal y scale (weight = 0.721), GPT4-Turbo prefers the chart on the left. This chart obtains a lower cost because DracoGPT-Rank has a stronger preference for encoding the variable of interest q1 with the x channel (weight = −1.964) and a continuous x scale (
    \$\text{weight} =-1.055\$
  ) for value tasks. Therefore, it is important to evaluate design preferences at the chart level to complement weight-level analysis.

An overlay grid of crosshairs and circles describes targets for each task: (A) Advect: Trace a path downhill from the center to the edge of a circle, (B) Compare: Find the point with the lowest elevation, and (C) Range: Find the minimum and maximum elevation inside the circle. Example ground-truth answers are notated with an asterisk (
    \$^{\star}\$
  ).
